---
Scope checked: .swarm/manifests/R1.3.files (internal/handlers/accounts/handlers.go,
internal/services/accounts/accounts.go, internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/anchor.go, and
their three new test files). Out of scope (R2/R3/R7) not touched by this review.

Regression 1 — HTTP 500->200 on load failure (handleDelete/handleAddAnchor/handleDeleteAnchor):
- Mechanism reviewed: Mutate's nil-storage guard (`if s == nil`) returns BEFORE mu.Lock/the
  closure runs, so `loaded` correctly stays false for that case too, matching HEAD's
  Load()-based nil-storage 500 (same underlying "accounts: nil storage" message either way —
  no behavior change there).
- A decode error and a genuine I/O error both surface from loadTx before fn runs, so both
  correctly land on the !loaded/500 branch, same as HEAD's Load() folding both into one err.
- saveTx failures (Validate or WriteFile) happen strictly AFTER fn has already set loaded=true
  (verified by reading Mutate's body: loadTx -> fn -> saveTx, in that order), so a save/
  validation failure still takes the loaded/200/renderList path. Confirmed with real tests:
  TestHandle{Delete,AddAnchor,DeleteAnchor}_SaveFailureStays200WithInlineError all pass against
  the actual repo (read-only store dir forces a write failure while load succeeds).
- Restored message is byte-identical: "Failed to load accounts: "+err.Error(), 500.
- My own reproduction: go test -run 'LoadFailure|SaveFailure' ./internal/handlers/accounts/...
  -v — all 6 tests PASS against the real tree.
- Mutation check (scratch copy outside repo, `if !loaded` -> `if false && !loaded`): all three
  LoadFailureIs500 tests fail (200 got, 500 wanted) while all three SaveFailure tests still
  pass — confirms the tests are pinned to this exact branch, not vacuous.

Regression 2 — OverlapWarnings dropped on write failure:
- saveTx: Validate runs first (unchanged order, matches SaveWithWarnings), THEN
  OverlapWarnings is computed and logged unconditionally, BEFORE marshal/WriteFile. A
  Validate failure still short-circuits before OverlapWarnings is ever computed/logged — no
  new side effect on validation failure (the specific inverse regression the brief flagged as
  a risk). A WriteFile failure now still logs, since the log statement runs before the write
  is attempted.
- TestMutate_LogsOverlapWarningsEvenWhenWriteFails passes against the real tree (read-only
  store dir, two overlapping patterns).
- Mutation check: reverting to log-after-WriteFile (attempt-2 shape) makes this test fail
  ("expected the overlap warning to be logged... got log output: \"\"").

Regression 3 — applyAnchor load-failure message folded into token-spent wording:
- anchor.go restores the distinct `loaded` bool exactly matching the pre-Mutate-refactor
  order confirmed via `git diff origin/fix/review-aug16 -- .../anchor.go`: Redeem -> ensureSnapshot
  -> Mutate, with the !loaded branch giving the byte-identical "cannot reload accounts before
  writing: %w" text and no snapNote/token-spent wording; the loaded-but-erred branch keeps the
  original snapNote-wrapped "confirmation token has been spent either way" wording.
  ensureSnapshot and Redeem still run BEFORE Mutate opens (unchanged control flow / token
  spend / snapshot timing).
- TestApplyAnchor_LoadFailureMessageIsDistinct and TestApplyAnchor_SaveFailureMessageIsUnchanged
  both pass against the real tree.
- Mutation check: reverting the !loaded branch makes the load-failure test fail with the
  token-spent wording; the save-failure test is unaffected — confirms non-vacuous, tied to
  message text not just presence of an error.

Non-vacuousness of all nine new tests: verified by count (6 + 1 + 2 = 9, matches the brief)
and by running all three representative mutation reversions myself in a scratch copy outside
the repo (not the actual worktree) — each reversion fails exactly the tests that should catch
it and none of the others. This satisfies the "revert and confirm the matching test fails"
requirement even though I found no separate worker-authored report file documenting it.

Concurrency untouched: read Mutate/loadTx/saveTx in full. Lock order matches storage.go's
contract as previously confirmed at attempt 2 (package `mu` outside BeginShared, tx's own
ReadFile/WriteFile used instead of Storage's plain methods, no cross-service call inside the
held section). The saveTx warnings-log fix is a reordering of a pure log statement inside the
already-held section — it does not add, remove, or reorder any lock/tx acquisition, so it
cannot affect the "BeginExclusive not granted while a Mutate section is open" guarantee.
ensureSnapshot in anchor.go remains outside Mutate, as before.

Oracle and full suite: `bash .swarm/tier3/R1/accept.sh` run fresh by me, exit 0. All six
steps pass, including go build, go vet, pinned Mutate signature grep, no unserialized
save/Load-outside-Mutate at the call sites, the lead oracle test under -race, and the FULL
suite under -race (including internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger, which passed — no R9 flake hit,
no rerun needed).

No counter-evidence found for the claim under test. All three regressions are repaired with
byte-identical restored messages/status codes, no inverse regression was introduced on the
save/validation paths, and the concurrency guarantees are intact.
